course: dictionary
lesson: 10230
title: Today: this day and these days
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word today can mean this day, the day that is happening now. It can also mean the present time, these days. Context tells you which meaning is right. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about one particular day, or about life right now?
explain: «In the old days poor children were taught to call richer people sir; today we'd say everyone deserves the same respect.» Here today does not mean this one day. It means now, at the present time, in contrast with the old days.
explain: Today can also be a noun, as in «today's lesson». Here it names the day you are in. Words like «until today» and «a week from today» show that today is a point in time that other things are measured from.
fact: Today means this day, the day that is happening now.
fact: Today can also mean the present time, these days, as in «Children today use tablets».
fact: Today can be an adverb, as in «live today», or a noun, as in «today's lesson».
fact: «A week from today» means seven days after this day.
fact: In Scotland, «the day» can mean today, as in the example «dreich» sentence about the weather.
exercise: «In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter; today giant mirrors and dishes see galaxies near the edge of the visible universe.» In this sentence, what does today mean? | *The present time, these days | A day of the week | Early in the morning | Yesterday
exercise: Mia says, «Today's lesson is about rivers.» What does today mean here? | Every week | Next year | *This day | Long ago
exercise: In Scotland, people say «the day» to mean which day? | Tomorrow | Yesterday | Last week | *Today
test: «Children today use tablets.» In this sentence, today means | Only this morning | Next Monday | Last year | *These days, the present time
test: Which phrase means seven days after this day? | *A week from today | Today a week ago | Last week's day | Yesterday week
exam: What does today mean in «about 476 million Indigenous people live today»? | *These days, the present time | This very day only | Long ago | Yesterday
